            "value": [
              {
                "dsDescriptionValue": {
                  "typeName": "dsDescriptionValue",
                  "multiple": false,
                  "typeClass": "primitive",
                  "value": "Mycoplasma pneumoniae (M. pneumoniae) is a common cause of pediatric respiratory infections. In summer 2023, M. pneumoniae re-emerged post-COVID-19. In this study we characterized the outbreak of M. pneumoniae in secondary and tertiary pediatric care in the Netherlands during the 2023-2024 epidemic. \n\nThe SPREAD-MYCO study is a prospective observational national multicenter study collecting prospective data of children (0-17 years) in 35 hospitals (emergency department/clinical ward) including all 7 pediatric intensive care units (PICUs) in the Netherlands. Weekly numbers of M. pneumoniae tests and clinical characteristics (subset) during the 2023/2024 epidemic were reported. The same data from the previous 2019/2020 epidemic were collected retrospectively."
                }
              }
            ]
          },
